--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THE WEB PAGE IS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SignalGapDetectorPage.tsx is a thin wrapper around the shared SignalCatalogPanel.
It sets a PageContainer (title=signalGap.title, subtitle=signalGap.subtitle,
actions=<VehicleSelect/>), reads the global useSelectedVehicle() store, and renders
a ternary: when no vehicle is selected (!vehicleId || vehicleId <= 0) it shows an
<EmptyState icon={<Activity/>} title=signalGap.noVehicle message=signalGap.noVehicleDesc/>;
otherwise it embeds <SignalCatalogPanel vehicleId/>. The page itself declares no data
of its own — the parity manifest records zero dataSources, zero panels, exactly one
data state (empty) and four strings (requiredCount=5). The embedded SignalCatalogPanel
owns the live-signals feed (useSignalGaps -> GET /signals/{id}/live) and all of its own
loading/empty/error/content states.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NATIVE IMPLEMENTATION (no placeholders, ADR-011; no delegation)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The shared A3 SignalCatalogPanel feature-view already exists
(io.teslasync.android.featureviews.signalcatalogpanel.SignalCatalogPanel) and owns the
summary StatCards, search/filter/sort controls, the staleness table, and every
cache-then-network state (loading / empty / filtered-empty / error+retry / content /
stale / offline). The shared VehicleSelect surface
(io.teslasync.android.sharedsurfaces.vehicleselect.VehicleSelect) is the store-bound
vehicle-scope picker. This page is their host: it sets the PageContainer-equivalent
header (title + subtitle + the VehicleSelect action), reads the resolved active-vehicle
scope through a page ViewModel bound to the shared P1/S8 selection + fleet holders, and
renders the web ternary — never re-implementing the catalog or the picker (DRY, ADR-006).
This mirrors the sibling notifications/ChannelsPage (a wrapper embedding
NotificationChannelsView) and driving/RegenEfficiencyPage (a host that builds a page-local
Http*Repository because the Android DI graph wires no domain store yet).

