Notes:
  - i18n catalog: signalGap.noVehicle / signalGap.noVehicleDesc are NOT in the web
    canonical en.json — the web page resolves them from inline t() fallback defaults
    ("Select a vehicle to begin" / "Pick a vehicle from the picker above to inspect its
    signal freshness."). en.json is outside this artifact's allowed files and there is no
    web catalog entry to mirror, so the Android catalog receives those exact inline-default
    values (honest disclosure; no silent drift). MissingTranslation/ExtraTranslation are
    disabled in the app lint config, so the ar/he English-fallback entries are accepted.
  - Routing: the destination page("signalGaps","/signal-gaps",NavGroup.Telemetry) already
    exists in Destinations.kt (metadata-only) with nav title nav_signal_gaps in NavStrings;
    this artifact only attaches the host (no route-table change), so RouteTableTest stays
    green.
  - Data wiring: the Android DI graph (DataContainer) wires no TelemetryStore, so the host
    builds a page-local HttpTelemetryRepository from the shared client + offline cache the
    container exposes (the RegenEfficiencyPageHost HttpDrivingRepository precedent). The
    view performs no HTTP.
  - SI: this page renders no unit-bearing field of its own; the embedded SignalCatalogPanel
    keeps raw SI and formats at its own boundary (Phase-42/48). No SI conversion here.
  - a11y/theme: PageTitle heading + BodyText subtitle via MaterialTheme tokens; EmptyState,
    VehicleSelect and SignalCatalogPanel supply their own content descriptions + dynamic/
    dark theme (ADR-015). No hardcoded colors/typography.

